 "model": "INMBSMIT050C000 / INMBSMIT100C000 Mitsubishi Electric City Multi centralised controller to Modbus gateway",
 "model_slug": "inmbsmit050c000",
 "short_model": "INMBSMIT050C000 Mitsubishi CC",
 "aliases": [
  "INMBSMIT050C000",
  "INMBSMIT100C000",
  "ME-AC-MBS-50",
  "ME-AC-MBS-100",
  "Intesis Modbus Server Mitsubishi Electric CC"
 ],
 "equipment_type": "VRF / split AC gateway",
 "applies_to": "Intesis Modbus Server - Mitsubishi Electric CC, order codes INMBSMIT050C000 / INMBSMIT100C000 (legacy ME-AC-MBS-50 / -100), user manual r1.4 (05/2021); talks to City Multi centralised controllers (G-50A, GB-50A, AG-150A, EB-50, EW-50, AE-200 and newer) through their XML interface over Ethernet.",
 "summary": "Modbus server that reads Mitsubishi Electric City Multi groups through one or two centralised controllers (XML over Ethernet). Each group (1..50 per controller) gets a 100-register block with on/off, mode, fan, vane, run hours, errors and local-panel permissions; each controller also has 26 all-group command registers. Covers indoor units, Lossnay, OA processing, ATW booster/HEX and CEh heat pumps.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU",
  "TCP"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": 502
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "The manual states formula results are link-layer addresses with the first register at 0. Controller signals: cc x 30 + signal; group signals: ((cc x 50) + g) x 100 + signal, with cc = 0 or 1 and g = group 1..50. This file lists cc = 0 (0..24) and cc 0 group 1 (100..137)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "Intesis Modbus Server - Mitsubishi Electric CC User Manual",
  "doc_number": "User Manual r1.4 EN",
  "revision_date": "2021-05",
  "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-inmbsmitxxxc000.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 7-12 (Modbus interface and address map)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Only controller 0 and its group 1 are listed. Group g on controller cc: add ((cc x 50) + g - 1) x 100 (cc 0 group 2 on/off = 200; cc 1 group 1 = 5100). Controller 1 signals: add 30.",
  "All temperature registers are left out (all-group setpoint cc x 30 + 25, group setpoint +4, ambient +5, setpoint restrictions +21..+26, multiple setpoints +27..+31, outdoor temperature +35): setpoints are printed as whole '°C' yet with half-degree ranges such as 4.5..35 °C, and ambient is printed '°C/x10°C' with a 0.0..99.9 range, so the scale cannot be fixed from the document.",
  "Mode, fan and setpoint registers have different meanings for Lossnay (LC), ATW booster/HEX and CEh heat-pump groups; only indoor-unit (IC) codes are decoded. Lossnay mode: 0 LC Auto, 1 Heat Recovery, 2 Bypass. ATW/HWHP mode: 0 Hot water, 1 Heating, 2 Heating Eco, 3 Anti-freeze, 4 Cooling.",
  "The IC fan-speed value list is printed as '0-Auto, 1-Low, 2-Mid-1, 3-Mid-2, 2-Mid2, 3-Mid1, 4-High', which assigns 2 and 3 twice; only 0, 1 and 4 are decoded. The Lossnay fan list is equally garbled and is not decoded.",
  "Which registers exist depends on the unit type selected in MAPS (IC, LC, FU, BU, WH, CEh); the manual's applicability matrix is not reproduced.",
  "Brightness and occupancy (+33 / +34) carry the same 'Setpoint Type = Multiple Setpoint' availability note as the setpoint rows in the manual."
 ],
